  "question": {
    "text": "Two identical wires <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math>, each of length <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>l</mi></math>, carry the same current <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>I</mi></math> . Wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>A</mi></math> is bent into a circle of radius <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>R</mi></math> and wire <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>B</mi></math> is bent to form a square of side <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>a</mi></math>. If <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub></math> and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></math> are the values of magnetic field at the centres of the circle and square respectively, then the ratio <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">A</mi></msub><msub><mi>B</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">B</mi></msub></mfrac></math> is",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "NTCUP",
      "text": "<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><msup><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">&#960;</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mn>16</mn></mfrac></math>",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
